One DevOps interview question that reveals real experience:

“Production is down. What do you check first?”

Many answers start with:

• checking logs
• restarting services
• rolling back deployments

But experienced engineers begin with one question:

👉 What changed recently?

Because most outages are triggered by:

• new deployments
• config updates
• infrastructure changes
• certificate expiry
• sudden traffic spikes

---

A simple troubleshooting flow:

1️⃣ Check recent deployments & changes
2️⃣ Look at error rates and system metrics
3️⃣ Correlate metrics with logs
4️⃣ Validate dependencies (DB, cache, external APIs)
5️⃣ Mitigate quickly, then fix the root cause

---

Anyone can run commands.

Great engineers understand failure.

Save this for your DevOps/SRE interviews.
